    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d520">

                <pb facs="0591" n="541" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg541"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Uhl to Mr. White.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-06-18"><hi rendition="#italic">June 18,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 208.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose copies of two letters<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d520-f1"/> received from Mr. W. W. Saperston and Mr. B. B.
                    Bloch, reporting the case of Stanislaus O. Krzeminski, a native of
                    Russian-Poland, and alleged to be a naturalized American citizen, who, on
                    returning to Russia during the spring of this year, is said to have been
                    arrested and, without trial, exiled to the salt mines in Siberia.</p>
                <p>I also inclose copy<anchor n="1" xml:id="d520-f2"/> of Department’s reply to Mr.
                    Saperston.</p>
                <p>You are instructed to investigate the case, and if Mr. Krzeminski’s American
                    citizenship be established and the facts warrant it, you will do everything in
                    your power to save this unfortunate man from the severe (and in the case of a
                    naturalized American citizen, extraordinary) penalty of exile to the Siberian
                    mines.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin F. Uhl</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
